{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"head -35 task/task.md; jq '{data,protocol,method,publication}' task/task_contract.json; jq '{sources,normalization,extraction,own_counts,split_rule,cross_plane_intersections}' task/resources/final/audit.json | head -160; jq '{within_plane_split_rule,production:(.production|keys)}' task/resources/final/plan.json; sed -n '22,90p' .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex; python .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py --global-memory-md \\\"\"'$(realpath global_memory)/memory.md\" --global-memory-jsonl \"$(realpath global_memory)/memory.jsonl\" --event-json '\"'{\\\"step\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Inspect final evidence independently and choose a retained masked-factor study, not an alternative-method success story.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"final.qualification.status=completed and final.qualification.outcome=qualified. Frozen baseline selected; study.search_score_delta=0; 0 scored and 3 unscored attempts. Selected and original baseline source files compare identical. Three final seeds provide source/split/matched-baseline/corruption evidence; candidate diagnostics unverified. ICLR style is single-column 5.5in by 9in with 8-9 body-page requirement. No edit context or prior manuscript is staged.\\\",\\\"next_action\\\":\\\"Check exact metric and target protocol; plan a direct conditional comparison and early overview with explicit limitations. Conclusions gate=keep because this is framing, not a new experimental finding.\\\",\\\"tags\\\":[\\\"framing\\\",\\\"sealed_final\\\",\\\"no_search_gain\\\",\\\"gate=keep\\\"]}'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"head -35 task/task.md; jq '{data,protocol,method,publication}' task/task_contract.json; jq '{sources,normalization,extraction,own_counts,split_rule,cross_plane_intersections}' task/resources/final/audit.json | head -160; jq '{within_plane_split_rule,production:(.production|keys)}' task/resources/final/plan.json; sed -n '22,90p' .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex; python .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py --global-memory-md \\\"\"'$(realpath global_memory)/memory.md\" --global-memory-jsonl \"$(realpath global_memory)/memory.jsonl\" --event-json '\"'{\\\"step\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Inspect final evidence independently and choose a retained masked-factor study, not an alternative-method success story.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"final.qualification.status=completed and final.qualification.outcome=qualified. Frozen baseline selected; study.search_score_delta=0; 0 scored and 3 unscored attempts. Selected and original baseline source files compare identical. Three final seeds provide source/split/matched-baseline/corruption evidence; candidate diagnostics unverified. ICLR style is single-column 5.5in by 9in with 8-9 body-page requirement. No edit context or prior manuscript is staged.\\\",\\\"next_action\\\":\\\"Check exact metric and target protocol; plan a direct conditional comparison and early overview with explicit limitations. Conclusions gate=keep because this is framing, not a new experimental finding.\\\",\\\"tags\\\":[\\\"framing\\\",\\\"sealed_final\\\",\\\"no_search_gain\\\",\\\"gate=keep\\\"]}'\"","aggregated_output":"# Goal\n\n**研究任务：用少量基准预测大模型在其余基准上的表现**\n**问题与动机**\n评估一个大语言模型通常要在几十乃至上百个基准（或子任务）上逐一运行，每个基准都消耗算力、时间和人力。\n与此同时，公开榜单积累了大量\"模型 × 基准\"的得分记录，不同基准的得分之间是否相关、相关到什么程度，是需要用数据回答的问题。\n\n设想一位评测者面对如下情形：\n\n- 手头有一张历史得分矩阵：M 个已评测模型、N 个基准，部分格子缺失（并非每个模型都跑过每个基准）；\n- 来了一个新模型，评测预算只允许在其中 k 个基准上实际运行（k 远小于 N）；\n- 评测者希望用这 k 个基准上的实测得分，尽可能准确地推断该模型在其余 N−k 个基准上的得分。\n\n**核心问题：在只能运行 k 个基准的预算下，应当如何选择这 k 个基准，并据此推断新模型在其余基准上的得分，才能使推断最准？需要多大的 k 才够用？**\n\n请你作为独立研究者：\n\n1. 梳理已有的相关做法与局限，明确你要回答的具体研究问题与假设；\n2. 提出并实现一套选择基准、并据此推断其余基准得分的方法，说明其适用条件与代价；\n3. 在公开榜单构成的真实得分矩阵上设计并运行实验：说明你的评估协议为什么能回答研究问题，与合适的基线对照，并说明结论在哪些数据条件下成立；\n4. 如能给出理论分析，请给出推导并用实验核对。\n\n**成功的衡量：** 以对新模型在未运行基准上的得分推断与其实测得分的接近程度来衡量。结论可以是你的假设得到支持、被反驳，或仅在部分数据条件下成立，均以实验证据为准。\n\n**约束：** 仅用 CPU 即可完成，时间上限一周，存储 < 5 GB；数据来自公开榜单（见 `data.md`）；产出为一篇研究论文及全部代码（见 `deliverable.md`）。\n\n以研究问题和实验证据为主线，自行决定具体路线。\n\n**起步文献清单**\n取证日期：2026-10-26。括号内为各条的首次提交日期。\n\n1. Hendrycks et al. *Measuring Massive Multitask Language Understanding.* arXiv:2009.03300（2020-09-07 首次提交）。https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.03300 。说明：提出覆盖 57 个学科（含初等数学、美国历史、计算机科学、法律等）的多选题基准，用于衡量文本模型的多任务准确率。\n2. Muennighoff, Tazi, Magne, Reimers. *MTEB: Massive Text Embedding Benchmark.* arXiv:2210.07316（2022-10-13）。https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.07316 。说明：提出覆盖 8 类嵌入任务、58 个数据集、112 种语言的文本嵌入评测基准，评测了 33 个模型，附开源代码和公开榜单。\n3. Liang et al. *Holistic Evaluation of Language Models.* arXiv:2211.09110（2022-11-16）。https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.09110 。说明：提出在多种使用场景、多项指标下对语言模型做统一评测的框架，并公开了对 30 个模型的评测结果以及原始提示与输出。\n4. Zheng et al. *Judging LLM-as-a-judge with MT-Bench and Chatbot Arena.* arXiv:2306.05685（2023-06-09）。https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.05685 。说明：研究用强语言模型作评判者评估对话助手，提出 MT-bench（多轮问题集）和 Chatbot Arena（众包对战平台），并考察评判者与人类偏好的一致程度。\n{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"final_roles\": [\n      \"sealed_history_queries_targets\",\n      \"sealed_controls_and_splits\"\n    ],\n    \"search_roles\": [\n      \"search_history_queries_targets\",\n      \"search_controls_and_splits\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"protocol\": {\n    \"baselines\": [\n      \"historical_constant\",\n      \"random_query_copy_offset\",\n      \"random_query_masked_lowrank\",\n      \"correlation_medoid_ridge\",\n      \"information_selected_ridge\"\n    ],\n    \"final_reset_sequence\": [\n      1009,\n      1013,\n      1019,\n      1009,\n      1013,\n      1019,\n      1009,\n      1013,\n      1019,\n      1009,\n      1013,\n      1019,\n      1009,\n      1013,\n      1019,\n      1009,\n      1013,\n      1019,\n      1009,\n      1013,\n      1019,\n      1009,\n      1013,\n      1019,\n      1009\n    ],\n    \"final_seeds\": [\n      1009,\n      1013,\n      1019\n    ],\n    \"final_smoke_reset_sequence\": [\n      1009,\n      1009,\n      1009,\n      1009,\n      1009,\n      1009,\n      1009,\n      1009,\n      1009\n    ],\n    \"promotion_rule\": \"At most3 idea cycles with at most1 production search evaluation each. Search eligibility is correct:true scientific execution validity, not comparative superiority or publication novelty. Rank eligible candidates by descending combined_score, exact ties earliest evaluated then lexicographic code SHA256. Freeze candidate/runtime/procedure before final. Harness owns promotion and publication. Every invocation: four ordered cases, actual then permuted, seed order within each condition; exactly one trailing replay reset of first seed as the last element of the declared full transcript. Arrays enumerate every reset including the sole replay; operation budgets include it. Draft smoke exactly first seed per case-condition plus the same single trailing replay. All reset records are global across clients/restarts.\",\n    \"search_proxies\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"leaderboard_offline_proxy\",\n        \"omits\": \"No new benchmark inference, model training, actual benchmark execution cost or universal sufficient-k claim; MTEB embedding tasks are not generative LLM evidence.\",\n        \"preserves\": \"Real observed scores, missingness, held-out model/family groups, k-limited sequential paid observations, fixed uncertainty and matched baselines and controls.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"draft_smoke\",\n        \"omits\": \"Only32 historical and4 eligible test rows,12 comparable MTEB columns,2 requested sweeps and first seed. Reduced smoke is compatibility only, not production qualification or candidate-ranking evidence.\",\n        \"preserves\": \"All four cases and both conditions, real-source loading, exact API, full k checkpoints, five baselines, nonvacuous input control, replay, fixed metric paths and CPU topology.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"search_reset_sequence\": [\n      17,\n      29,\n      43,\n      17,\n      29,\n      43,\n      17,\n      29,\n      43,\n      17,\n      29,\n      43,\n      17,\n      29,\n      43,\n      17,\n      29,\n      43,\n      17,\n      29,\n      43,\n      17,\n      29,\n      43,\n      17\n    ],\n    \"search_seeds\": [\n      17,\n      29,\n      43\n    ],\n    \"search_smoke_reset_sequence\": [\n      17,\n      17,\n      17,\n      17,\n      17,\n      17,\n      17,\n      17,\n      17\n    ]\n  },\n  \"method\": {\n    \"class\": \"CPU_missingness_aware_benchmark_selection_prediction\",\n    \"description\": \"Fit masked low-rank score models and sequentially purchase up to k benchmark values per unseen model. MTEB checkpoints [1,2,4,8], OpenLLM [1,2,3], model/family-disjoint cases, 3 seeds each, actual and column-deranged training conditions, one trailing first-episode replay. Natural [0,1] MAE; target -> row -> checkpoint -> seed -> case -> source equal weights. Negative/inconclusive findings are legitimate: search.correct and final.correct require scientific execution validity, never beating a baseline. Final comparative claim assessment is separate. Production uses all eligible rows of pinned real sources, not synthetic stand-ins. CPython 3.12.15 Linux x86_64 validated; compatible Python>=3.11, no GPU or paid API. Native Landlock ABI>=1 and seccomp mandatory; 1 evaluator BLAS thread and up to3 candidate threads. No canonical minimum productive-baseline time is specified. Full score/operation-count tables, priors, fixed penalties and limitations are frozen in each resource plan.json. Largest declared complete request and response measured including base64, metadata, newline and 4096-byte extra envelope reserve. No state telemetry or mechanism claims from self-reports.\"\n  },\n  \"publication\": {\n    \"required_evidence\": [\n      \"Complete fixed production real-source episodes, baselines and nonvacuous controls, finite retained failure contributions, correct:true validity and single reproducible reset replay; smoke alone insufficient.\",\n      \"Pinned source versions and license/access caveats, normalized raw-document and complete model-example hash disjointness, alias/family and 70/30 within-plane splits, historical-only fitting and availability-conditioned eligibility; no resource-path RPC.\",\n      \"Actual selection and prediction method/code plus k-query ledgers and evaluator-computed error-versus-k/uncertainty; no candidate state or method-name self-report evidence. Comparisons must disclose ties, negative results, missing evidence and observational missingness.\",\n      \"Final superiority claims require positive paired family-clustered uncertainty against random lowrank, constant/copy and named reconstruction/selection ablations as appropriate; historical-structure attribution also requires supportive nonvacuous corruption control. No positive outcome is mandatory or retroactively a search gate.\",\n      \"Independent permitted literature review without searching/inferencing forbidden prior paper; actual experiment logs, reproducible data acquisition and code, environment versions, seeds, table/figure scripts, truthful failures and incomplete runs. Full paper PDF and LaTeX in latest official selected conference template with page-limit/checklist compliance; manual scientific review remains required.\",\n      \"Hard CPU/wall/memory/storage/RPC enforcement and broker transcripts are harness-owned. Native smoke validates bounded isolated transport but does not certify broker authentication or hidden candidate internals. No invented telemetry API.\"\n    ],\n    \"requires_final_evaluation\": true,\n    \"search_is_proxy\": true\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"sources\": {\n    \"mteb\": {\n      \"repository\": \"https://github.com/embeddings-benchmark/results\",\n      \"revision\": \"6dabbcc68c28ea5f180ce7df79347b3ca9cc6383\",\n      \"archive_sha256\": \"84773e577197630206eacc1790c5fd793d21393b698f6562b0a8f0a1ea31002f\",\n      \"license\": \"CC0-1.0 per task.md; pinned repository contains no standalone license file; no model inference or benchmark corpus included\"\n    },\n    \"open_llm\": {\n      \"repository\": \"https://huggingface.co/datasets/open-llm-leaderboard/contents\",\n      \"revision\": \"9c09a7cae43334062a82cb164f2ef255013dafa2\",\n      \"parquet_sha256\": \"f13a7061e63133bc8745d89f8c7a56148584940ede22d3b27e21cad1e078dca5\",\n      \"license\": \"Undeclared dataset license. Public unauthenticated access; private research extraction only, no asserted redistribution rights. Reacquire pinned public parquet for independent reproduction.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"normalization\": \"NFKC, LF, whitespace-collapse before split; canonical finite JSON; identifiers omitted from complete score-example hashes\",\n  \"extraction\": \"MTEB original test main_score in natural [0,1], default/English subsets only, distinct task/dataset_revision/subset columns; deterministic lexicographic first revision on repeated model-column; omit nonfinite/out-of-bound scores, no score-based filtering beyond declared natural bounds. OLL six Raw columns, no aggregates. Raw file hashes retained; model example hashes use complete extracted scores before preprocessing. Exact duplicate raw MTEB documents retain lexicographic archive-first owner only; other copies excluded as missing before splitting. Family is namespace plus lowercase model stem before first punctuation/digit, from OLL Base Model when present. OLL complete table read: 4576 source rows. Full eligible production rows used.\",\n  \"own_counts\": {\n    \"examples\": 2846,\n    \"documents\": 23743,\n    \"ids\": 2838,\n    \"families\": 732\n  },\n  \"split_rule\": \"Connected family/alias/complete-score-example/raw-document groups; SHA256(plane-v1/min(source/id)) parity\",\n  \"cross_plane_intersections\": {\n    \"examples\": 0,\n    \"documents\": 0,\n    \"ids\": 0,\n    \"families\": 0\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"within_plane_split_rule\": \"Deterministic 70/30 shuffle of connected normalized model-alias, raw-document hash and complete-example hash components across the plane; family links additionally merged in family-disjoint cases. Validate each component is contained in its acquisition group. Assert empty historical/test content and alias intersections before coverage or feature construction.\",\n  \"production\": [\n    \"cases\",\n    \"episodes\",\n    \"reset_sequence\",\n    \"rpc_total\"\n  ]\n}\n\\usepackage{url}\n\n\\title{Grounded Experimental Summary}\n\\iclrfinalcopy\n\\author{The Agentic Scientist}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nReplace with a concise grounded abstract summarizing setup, core result, and takeaway.\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\section{Introduction}\nReplace with grounded motivation, problem framing, and contributions.\n\n\\section{Related Work}\nSummarize relevant prior work using citation keys present in references.bib (for example, \\citep{templateReference2026}).\n\n\\section{Method}\nDescribe data, setup, and method details needed for reproducibility.\n\n\\section{Results}\nReport grounded quantitative and qualitative findings. Include figures and tables when useful.\n\n\\section{Conclusion}\nState key findings, limitations, and next steps supported by evidence.\n\n% IMPORTANT: \\clearpage flushes all pending floats before references so that\n% body-page counting excludes reference-only pages.  Do NOT remove.\n\\clearpage\n\\bibliography{references}\n\\bibliographystyle{paper}\n\n\\clearpage\n\\appendix\n\\section{Supplementary Information}\n% REQUIRED: Replace this scaffold with substantive grounded content.\n\\subsection{Reproducibility Details}\nReplace with grounded extended methods, reproducibility details, additional analyses, or supporting tables and figures.\n\n\\end{document}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
