{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'apply_patch() { codex --codex-run-as-apply-patch \"$1\"; }\napply_patch \"$(cat <<'\"'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /workspace/paper/paper_strategy.json\n+{\n+  \\\"status\\\": \\\"ready\\\",\n+  \\\"selected_prompt_family\\\": \\\"paper_standalone\\\",\n+  \\\"recommended_title\\\": \\\"Variance-Guided Benchmark Selection with Masked Low-Rank Score Models\\\",\n+  \\\"central_question\\\": \\\"Under limited benchmark-query budgets, how well does variance-guided selection with masked low-rank reconstruction predict held-out models' remaining observed scores across model-disjoint and name-family-disjoint leaderboard splits?\\\",\n+  \\\"central_thesis\\\": \\\"On the two pinned leaderboard matrices, the retained variance-guided low-rank method has a higher pooled remaining-target prediction score than the tested baselines and loses score under historical-column derangement, supporting a conditional empirical result rather than universal benchmark sufficiency, response-adaptive selection, or fixed-target superiority.\\\",\n+  \\\"narrative_rationale\\\": \\\"The strongest evidence is the sealed final comparison of one retained method against five operational baselines across two sources, two split regimes, and three seeds, with a paired uncertainty interval against random-query low-rank prediction and a dependence-destroying control. Present MTEB embedding tasks and Open LLM generative-model benchmarks as separate evidence blocks under a shared score-matrix question; fit each source independently, without cross-source model alignment or transfer claims. The contribution is a transparent empirical assessment and reproducible mechanism description, not a newly discovered winning architecture. The alternatives have no measured performance evidence. The informative limitations, especially method-dependent remaining targets and non-response-adaptive selection, belong in the central argument rather than only in the supplement.\\\",\n+  \\\"prior_paper_story_status\\\": \\\"rejected\\\",\n+  \\\"edit_framing_decision\\\": \\\"Fresh framing, not an edit: no resolved edit-context files, previous_paper manuscript, aggregated directory, or extra_tasks directory are staged. The status 'rejected' records that no inherited manuscript story is adopted; it does not reject a scientific result. Preserve-with-local-updates has no prior manuscript to preserve; broaden-to-a-shared-method-family is unsupported for the unscored alternative implementations; recenter-on-the-retained-evaluated-method is selected because it has direct final evidence. No old title or figure plan is carried forward.\\\",\n+  \\\"staged_input_impact\\\": [\n+    \\\"Direct inspection of source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py establishes masked alternating ridge factors, historical-cell rank selection, conditional ridge reconstruction, and set-conditioned variance-reduction querying; purchased values affect prediction but not query choice.\\\",\n+    \\\"The staged selected and original-baseline source files are byte-identical. Study selection is the original baseline, not an improved search winner; do not manufacture a second final comparator for the same source.\\\",\n+    \\\"The final evidence supplies the actual scientific comparison despite the absence of scored search alternatives. The final qualification record is read independently of the downstream selection summary.\\\",\n+    \\\"The pinned final audit, plan, task contract, and evaluator's scoring/baseline definitions explain the two data domains, remaining-target score, heuristic family grouping, budgets, and bootstrap semantics. They are protocol provenance, not additional experimental results or substitute quantitative grounding IDs.\\\",\n+    \\\"The current bibliography/provenance contains retrieved factorization-related metadata but lacks the permitted starter and dataset records needed for domain positioning. This limits literature claims, not the coherence of the measured comparison; the writer must verify relevant allowed records before citing them and must not fill pages with unrelated retrieval hits. No network retrieval is performed in this framing stage.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"method_groups\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Variance-guided masked low-rank reconstruction\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"proposed\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"The single studied method. Describe 'proposed' only as the contract role, not a novelty or search-improvement claim. The retained source learns masked factors and selects queries using a conditional trace-reduction proxy. Ground performance in final.evidence.episodes and final.metric.combined_score.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Random-query masked low-rank reconstruction\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"ablation\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"The closest selector comparison: source inspection confirms the same factor-fitting and prediction construction with random available queries. A pooled paired family-clustered interval is available against this comparator; different remaining targets still prevent a fixed-target causal interpretation.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Information-selected covariance ridge\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Strongest pooled nonfactor comparator. It changes representation, regularization selection, and potentially query sets, so it is a joint pipeline comparison rather than a matched-query reconstruction ablation. Retain the Open LLM family-split seed where it slightly exceeds the studied method.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Correlation-medoid covariance ridge\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Tests a simpler correlation-centrality query ordering with covariance reconstruction; provides an interpretable selection comparator without adding an unevaluated method family.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Historical benchmark means\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Observation-invariant reference for the substantial predictability already present in historical task means. Its operational score is computed on its own query-policy remainder, not a universal zero-query target set.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Random-query mean-offset prediction\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Simple purchased-score reference: shift historical benchmark means by the observed mean residual. Distinguishes structured reconstruction from a global model-level offset.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"results_focus\\\": [\n+    \\\"Primary view: final noncontrol, nonreplay case scores for the six methods, stratified by source and split, with all three seed observations visible. Label the metric 'Normalized prediction score (1 - MAE; higher is better)', not percent accuracy or variance explained. Average only with the documented equal target/row/checkpoint/seed/split/source hierarchy.\\\",\n+    \\\"Pooled evidence: studied method 0.9527636891226994, random-query low-rank 0.9364101694132948, information-selected ridge 0.9482262260487015, medoid ridge 0.9327472829724573, mean-offset 0.920605668187274, and historical means 0.90687688776656. Use a compact table, not a redundant figure. Only the studied-versus-random-low-rank comparison has a supplied paired interval: [0.014807167765235746, 0.01847801943997085]. Do not attach that interval to another comparator or a source/split cell.\\\",\n+    \\\"Source evidence remains distinct: MTEB pooled score 0.9468974985138557 and Open LLM pooled score 0.9586298797315429 describe different task and budget regimes, not a controlled difficulty comparison. MTEB is embedding-model evidence, not evidence about generative LLM benchmark suites.\\\",\n+    \\\"Dependence control: compare actual and independently column-deranged historical training scores for each source/split with paired seeds; pooled deranged score 0.9233917542059907 and actual-minus-deranged score 0.029371934916708625. The control supports dependence on historical alignment, not unique causal attribution to the acquisition rule or immunity to leakage.\\\",\n+    \\\"Qualification for claims: the factor method is not best in every retained cell. In Open LLM family split seed 1019, its 0.9531041725072664 is below information-selected ridge's 0.9533160599665489. Report this local reversal and avoid blanket or significant-superiority claims over all baselines.\\\",\n+    \\\"Budget evidence is descriptive: retain existing studied-method checkpoint values as an appendix table, with actual budget labels taken from the frozen final plan. No per-budget baseline series, fixed-target scores, tolerance-defined sufficient-k result, new inference-cost measurements, or missingness-sweep results are available.\\\",\n+    \\\"Private-only provenance: study.selection_kind=baseline; study.investigation_outcome=completed_no_winner; study.search_score_delta=0.0; study.attempts.total=3, scored=0, unscored=3. These establish no measured search gain and no comparative losses for alternative methods. Search and final scores must not be subtracted as improvement.\\\",\n+    \\\"Private-only qualification: final.qualification.status=completed, final.qualification.outcome=qualified, final.qualification.correct=true. There is no failed final qualification to disclose in this run. Detailed gate diagnostics are not supplied; qualification does not establish novelty, universal generalization, or validity of stronger scientific interpretations. Candidate diagnostics remain unverified.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_plan\\\": [\n+    \\\"Figure 1, early overview: sparse historical score matrix -> masked factor fit -> budgeted query set and purchased values -> remaining-score reconstruction, with distinct arrows showing that values update predictions but not selection; a small footer names the two source domains and two split regimes without numerical pseudo-results.\\\",\n+    \\\"Figure 2, main comparison: four horizontal dot-plot panels, arranged by source and split, compare all six evaluated methods using actual/nonreplay case scores; display three seed points and a clearly distinguished mean per method.\\\",\n+    \\\"Figure 3, dependence control: two source panels compare actual versus column-deranged historical training in each split using paired seed observations; use no training-time or search-trajectory axis.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_specs\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"concept_overview\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Make the score-matrix object, query/prediction mechanism, and boundaries of the evidence legible before the numerical comparisons.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"diagram\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"generate-concept-figure\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"information_flow\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"none; qualitative mechanism only\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"independent source-specific fits, not merged datasets\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"The inspected ICLR article template and paper.sty are single-column with 5.5in text width and 9in text height. Target 5.5 x 1.7in before caption, approximately one quarter page including caption, on page 1 or 2. Use one left-to-right schematic with at most six short labeled elements and 9pt minimum final text; a half-width inset would force small matrix labels. Any example cells use masks or symbolic values, never invented measured scores.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 6,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"study.selection_kind\\\"],\n+      \\\"implementation_provenance\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py\\\", \\\"task/resources/final/plan.json\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"main_comparison\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Show the direct six-method comparison and its source/split/seed heterogeneity, including the retained local reversal.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"horizontal_dot_plot\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"six evaluated method labels\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"normalized prediction score (1 - MAE), averaged across available checkpoints within each case\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"source by model-disjoint or name-family-disjoint split\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Target the actual single-column full text width, 5.5in, with a 2-by-2 grid approximately 3.7in tall before caption and at least 8.5pt final labels. Budget roughly half a body page including caption. Use short method labels with a shared expansion key, six horizontal rows per panel, and common score-axis semantics. Show three seed markers plus one mean marker, not six overlapping colored lines. A 0.48-textwidth placement would leave too little space for method labels and score differences. If a nonzero axis range is used, show it explicitly and use dots, not truncated bars.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 6,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"data_filter\\\": \\\"Keep control=false and replay=false only; do not double-count the first-seed replay; derive displayed means transparently from the retained episode scores, without treating them as new experiments.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"historical_dependence_control\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Expose how scores change when historical cross-benchmark correspondence is disrupted, with source and split heterogeneity visible.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"paired_condition_dot_plot\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"model-disjoint and name-family-disjoint split\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"normalized prediction score (1 - MAE)\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"MTEB embedding models versus Open LLM generative models\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Use two side-by-side source panels at the inspected 5.5in text width, approximately 2.1in tall before caption and 8.5pt minimum final text; reserve about 0.3 body page including caption. Two conditions and two split categories fit without rotating labels. Link paired seed observations only to mark the controlled contrast, not temporal progression. Do not shrink to half width or add five baseline control series.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.permuted_score\\\", \\\"final.metric.corruption_gap\\\"],\n+      \\\"data_filter\\\": \\\"Pair actual/control cases by source, split, and seed; exclude replay; use actual and column-deranged as the only condition legend entries.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"supplementary_plan\\\": {\n+    \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"After the references, provide reproducible implementation and protocol depth plus the complete retained numerical evidence, without moving central caveats, the main baseline contrast, or the dependence control out of the body.\\\",\n+    \\\"planned_subsections\\\": [\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Masked Factor Estimation and Conditional Querying\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Expand the inspected source into the masked squared-error/ridge objective, fixed column means, zero-filled centered initialization, alternating ridge updates, historical-cell rank selection, conditional prediction, and exact acquisition proxy. Explain that selection ignores observed values and includes the candidate coordinate in its current-target trace proxy. An algebraic rank-one covariance identity may explain the implementation; do not invent a recovery, optimality, or MAE guarantee. Use the staged source as implementation provenance, not as measured evidence of superiority.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"study.selection_kind\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Pinned Data Extraction, Grouping, and Reproduction\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Document the already-staged audit, plan, task contract, environment requirements, exact public source revisions, score extraction and bounds, deduplication, historical-only feature construction, heuristic name-family links, and checkpoint budgets. Preserve MTEB versus generative-model distinctions and the undeclared Open LLM dataset-license limitation. Provide exact rerun and table/figure-generation commands from the available implementation; do not invent scripts, measured storage, or timings. Treat audit/plan metadata as protocol provenance and register its evidence linkage before claiming any extra numerical dataset counts.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"study.selection_kind\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.qualification.status\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Complete Seed, Split, and Budget Tables\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Tabulate every nonreplay actual and control case, all five available baseline scores, and the studied method's retained checkpoint arrays. Map checkpoint positions to the frozen plan; do not infer absent per-budget baseline values. Include the local information-selected-ridge reversal. Mark seed variation as observed variation, not an independent-sample confidence interval, and state that missing cells were not prediction targets.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Aggregation, Uncertainty, and Evaluation Boundaries\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Explain equal aggregation weights and the supplied paired family-clustered bootstrap interval against random-query low-rank prediction, using the fixed plan's resampling definition. Retain the supplied interval rather than recomputing it from seed means. Describe remaining-target policy differences, absence of fixed-target controls, heuristic family labels, observational missingness, historical-cell rather than nested family validation, and lack of uncertainty for other baseline contrasts. Separate execution/replay checks from broader scientific validity.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.metric.paired_gain_ci_low\\\", \\\"final.metric.paired_gain_ci_high\\\", \\\"final.metric.reset_replay_ok\\\", \\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Unmeasured Alternatives and Evaluation Provenance\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Briefly disclose that the retained source was the original baseline, no search-score change was measured, and all alternative attempts lack scores. Their recorded execution failures have unknown causes and do not establish inferiority or a diagnosed validity/adaptivity defect. Preserve independent final completion/qualification facts and distinguish search from final evaluation; keep machine field names and local paths out of reader-facing prose. Do not create an alternative-method leaderboard.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"study.selection_kind\\\", \\\"study.investigation_outcome\\\", \\\"study.search_score_delta\\\", \\\"study.attempts.total\\\", \\\"study.attempts.scored\\\", \\\"study.attempts.unscored\\\", \\\"final.qualification.status\\\", \\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\", \\\"final.qualification.correct\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"LLM Usage\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Disclose the documented role of LLM agents in alternative-method ideation/implementation and this framing/writing workflow. Distinguish unscored generated alternatives from evaluated retained code; do not assert that an LLM trained the evaluated models, ran unrecorded experiments, or independently verified literature. The writing-stage author must add its actual role without inventing undocumented human supervision.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"study.attempts.total\\\", \\\"study.attempts.unscored\\\", \\\"study.selection_kind\\\"]\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \\\"forbidden_headings\\\": [\n+    \\\"Search Progression\\\",\n+    \\\"Campaign Phases\\\",\n+    \\\"Milestones\\\",\n+    \\\"First Successful Run\\\",\n+    \\\"Experiment A / Experiment B\\\",\n+    \\\"Candidate Leaderboard\\\",\n+    \\\"From Baseline to Winner\\\",\n+    \\\"Correctness and Eligibility\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"forbidden_phrases\\\": [\n+    \\\"we then tried\\\",\n+    \\\"first valid result\\\",\n+    \\\"subsequent improvements\\\",\n+    \\\"next-best candidate\\\",\n+    \\\"winning search method\\\",\n+    \\\"all alternatives performed worse\\\",\n+    \\\"correctness rate\\\",\n+    \\\"correct and eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_01\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_02\\\",\n+    \\\"combined_score\\\",\n+    \\\"rubric\\\",\n+    \\\"state of the art\\\",\n+    \\\"response-adaptive benchmark selection\\\",\n+    \\\"a universal sufficient number of benchmarks\\\",\n+    \\\"proved leakage-free\\\",\n+    \\\"significantly better than every baseline\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"notes_for_writer\\\": [\n+    \\\"The memo and source identifiers are private planning material. Reader-facing prose should use named methods, normalized prediction score, model-disjoint/name-family-disjoint splits, and column-deranged history. Do not expose machine-native metric labels, selection machinery, or local infrastructure paths.\\\",\n+    \\\"Private-only grounding ledger: primary metrics use final.metric.* and cases use final.evidence.episodes. Selection, search-score equality/delta, and attempt counts use study.*. Qualification uses final.qualification.* exclusively, not study.final.* or search execution flags. These records report completed/qualified/true in this run; do not invent a qualification failure or infer missing gate details. A later outcome change must propagate through draft, review, audit, and revision, not be hidden by retained metrics.\\\",\n+    \\\"Main-body structure and inclusive page targets: title/abstract 0.45 page; Introduction with early overview 1.05; Related Work 0.65; Problem and Scope 0.65; Masked Low-Rank Selection and Reconstruction 1.65; Evaluation Design 1.0; Prediction and Historical-Dependence Results 1.8; Discussion and Limitations 0.95; Conclusion 0.30. Total target 8.5 body pages, with figures/tables included in those allocations, not added afterward. The hard venue range is 8-9 pages excluding references; an 8-page body needs its last page at least 75% full. Use extra space for equations, baseline definitions, aggregation and target-policy explanation, not unmeasured experiments or broad literature filler.\\\",\n+    \\\"The template is single-column: column width and full text width are both 5.5in, not a two-column 0.48-textwidth convention. Use ordinary figure environments at the planned full width. Text height is 9in. The supplied paper.tex scaffold has an identifying author and final-copy command: the future writer must anonymize it and use review formatting as required by VENUE.md, preserve the orchestrator watermark, and not claim the locally staged style has been independently verified as the latest official release.\\\",\n+    \\\"Report the objective exactly: clip predictions to [0,1], score only available unpurchased entries, and average absolute errors within each model before the frozen hierarchy. High scores are not classification accuracy, percent of benchmarks recovered, calibrated uncertainty, or explained variance. Querying changes the target set; observed objectives cannot establish error reduction on an identical held-out panel.\\\",\n+    \\\"A mechanistic account may derive the implemented conditional covariance/ridge equations under a working linear model. Explicitly distinguish the acquisition trace proxy from MAE optimality and from a pure off-diagonal target-risk criterion. The studied selector is sequential but does not depend on purchased score values. Do not attribute it to the unscored overlap-shrunk, latent-mixture, or monotone-skill proposals.\\\",\n+    \\\"No new ablations, fixed-target evaluations, family-validation results, nonlinear wins, rank-sensitivity sweeps, calibration curves, real benchmark execution savings, GPU comparisons, or universal k thresholds may be planned as completed evidence. Budget tables answer only what the retained checkpoint scores show; no error-tolerance target was prespecified.\\\",\n+    \\\"The supplied paired interval supports only the pooled comparison with random-query low-rank prediction under the observed objective. For all other comparisons use observed-score language and display seed variability without inventing p-values or confidence intervals. Do not count replay as a fourth seed or assume three seeds are independent model families.\\\",\n+    \\\"Historical derangement preserves marginal/missingness structure while disrupting row correspondence; a score drop supports use of cross-benchmark alignment, not proof of a unique mechanism, generalization to arbitrary models, or an exhaustive validity audit. Family links are naming heuristics; MTEB and Open LLM are independent source-specific fits.\\\",\n+    \\\"Keep all central comparisons, the actual-versus-deranged control, and essential caveats in the main text. Route full case/checkpoint tables, expanded equations, acquisition/environment details and documented unmeasured alternatives after references under Supplementary Information. Any later authoritative appendix ranking may add material there without changing this strategy.\\\",\n+    \\\"Vector-first contract: quantitative generators must export both PDF and PNG from the same source, PNG at 300 DPI; LaTeX must include PDF whenever available. Preserve editable draw.io and PDF exports for the concept overview. If raster-only is unavoidable, regenerate from source at least 2400px wide for these full-width figures, or 1200px for any genuine column-width alternative; never upscale an existing raster. Inspect final-size labels and simplify rather than shrink. Use at most one generate-concept-figure diagram.\\\",\n+    \\\"Literature guardrail: the current retrieved metadata is not a read/verified domain literature review. Cite only relevant keys actually present in references.bib after checking their provenance and permitted content. Missing starter/data records require narrowly scoped exact-title or exact-identifier resolution and actual reading before citation; never search for the forbidden prior study, traverse citation graphs, guess its identity, or invent missing entries. Log and stop reading any incidental forbidden material. Do not import the retrieval list's unrelated application papers merely to satisfy page count.\\\",\n+    \\\"Contribution wording should emphasize a reproducible empirical study of a retained method and operational limits, not a new architecture or search success. Publication-format compliance is separate from scientific qualification. No final manuscript, evidence-claim map, final-paper validation, or new experiments are produced in this strategy stage.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"failure_reason\\\": \\\"\\\"\n+}\n*** Add File: /workspace/paper/paper_strategy.md\n+# Paper Framing Strategy\n+\n+## Decision\n+\n+**Status: ready.** Use \"'`paper_standalone` and the `write-paper-standalone` family. Provisional title: **Variance-Guided Benchmark Selection with Masked Low-Rank Score Models**.\n+\n+**Central question:** Under limited benchmark-query budgets, how well does variance-guided selection with masked low-rank reconstruction predict held-out models'\"' remaining observed scores across model-disjoint and name-family-disjoint leaderboard splits?\n+\n+**Central thesis:** On the two pinned leaderboard matrices, the retained variance-guided low-rank method has a higher pooled remaining-target prediction score than the tested baselines and loses score under historical-column derangement, supporting a conditional empirical result rather than universal benchmark sufficiency, response-adaptive selection, or fixed-target superiority.\n+\n+This is an empirical assessment of one retained method, not a story about inventing a winning architecture. MTEB embedding models and Open LLM generative models form **separate evidence blocks under one score-matrix question**. Fit and discuss them independently; do not claim cross-source transfer, merge their model identities, or treat embedding tasks as generative-model benchmarks.\n+\n+## Framing Alternatives and Staged Inputs\n+\n+No resolved edit-context files, prior manuscript, \"'`aggregated/`, or `extra_tasks/` are staged. `prior_paper_story_status` is `rejected`: no inherited story is adopted, not a rejection of an old scientific result.\n+\n+- **Preserve with local updates:** inapplicable because there is no prior manuscript to preserve.\n+- **Broaden to a shared alternative-method family:** rejected because overlap-shrunk covariance, latent mixtures, and monotone-skill alternatives have no measured performance evidence.\n+- **Recenter on the retained evaluated method:** selected because it alone has final evidence with meaningful baseline, split, seed, and corruption comparisons.\n+- **Center a negative search-results paper:** weaker than the selected framing. Unscored alternatives do not establish measured negative performance findings, whereas the retained method has an actual comparative evaluation.\n+\n+Direct inspection of `source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py` establishes masked alternating ridge factors, historical-cell rank selection, conditional ridge prediction, and a trace-reduction query proxy. The selected and original-baseline staged source files are byte-identical. The method is sequential and set-conditioned: purchased score values affect reconstruction **but not query choice**. It is not the response-adaptive mixture or the off-diagonal overlap-aware proposal.\n+\n+The frozen audit and plan under `task/resources/final/`, the task contract, and the evaluator'\"'s score/baseline definitions provide protocol provenance. They do not substitute for registered numerical result sources. Do not assert equality between differently recorded whole-tree hashes merely from equality of the staged source files.\n+\n+## Private-Only Evidence Ledger\n+\n+This section is planning/audit context, not reader-facing vocabulary.\n+\n+- Read \"'`paper_data.json.final_evaluation` independently. `final.qualification.status` is `completed`, `final.qualification.outcome` is `qualified`, and `final.qualification.correct` is true. There is **no failed final qualification** to disclose in this run. Detailed gate diagnostics remain unavailable; successful completion does not establish scientific novelty or stronger validity claims. Candidate diagnostics are explicitly unverified.\n+- Selection uses `study.selection_kind=baseline` and `study.investigation_outcome=completed_no_winner`. Both search score and original-baseline score are 0.9527030000575736; `study.search_score_delta=0.0`.\n+- `study.attempts.total=3`, `study.attempts.scored=0`, and `study.attempts.unscored=3`. Unscored attempts are missing performance evidence, not measured losses. Their recorded execution-failure causes are unknown; neither inferiority nor a particular validity/adaptivity defect is diagnosed.\n+- Keep search and final scopes separate. Never subtract the search score from the final score and call it improvement. Do not display the frozen source as an improved replacement for its identical original baseline.\n+- Final case data come from `final.evidence.episodes`. The three final seeds are 1009, 1013, and 1019. Exclude control cases from primary comparisons and exclude the replay from every primary aggregate; replay is not a fourth seed.\n+- Qualification statements must map to `final.qualification.*`, not downstream mirrors or search flags. If later evidence changes the outcome, preserve the changed qualification and its limitations in drafting, review, audit, and revision.\n+\n+## Method Groups\n+\n+Keep exactly the six evaluated plot labels; group them scientifically rather than by discovery order.\n+\n+| Group | Role | Scientific purpose |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Variance-guided masked low-rank reconstruction | Studied method; `proposed` in the JSON contract only | Connect incomplete historical scores, conditional reconstruction, and variance-guided queries; do not imply new architecture or a search gain. |\n+| Random-query masked low-rank reconstruction | Selector ablation | Same factor-fitting/prediction construction, different query rule; closest comparison and only comparator with supplied pooled paired uncertainty. |\n+| Information-selected covariance ridge | Strong baseline | Closest pooled nonfactor comparator; representation, tuning, and queries can all differ, so not a matched-query prediction ablation. |\n+| Correlation-medoid covariance ridge | Simpler baseline | Historical correlation-centrality ordering with covariance reconstruction. |\n+| Historical benchmark means | Observation-invariant baseline | Expose predictable task marginals; its evaluated remainder still depends on its operational query policy. |\n+| Random-query mean-offset prediction | Simple observation-using baseline | Test whether a single model-level score offset explains the result. |\n+\n+Do not add unevaluated methods to the performance comparison. A short supplementary disclosure of alternatives is sufficient.\n+\n+## Results and Claim Boundaries\n+\n+### Primary comparison\n+\n+Show the six methods in each source-by-split condition, displaying every retained seed score. The reader-facing metric is **Normalized prediction score (1 − MAE; higher is better)**. Predictions are clipped to natural score bounds; errors are averaged over available, unpurchased entries within a model and then through the frozen checkpoint/seed/split/source hierarchy. This is not classification accuracy, explained variance, or the fraction of benchmarks successfully recovered.\n+\n+The pooled scores below already exist in `paper_data.json`; use their `final.metric.*` sources in the eventual claim map.\n+\n+| Method | Pooled score | Grounding ID |\n+| --- | ---: | --- |\n+| Variance-guided masked low-rank | 0.9527636891226994 | `final.metric.combined_score` |\n+| Random-query masked low-rank | 0.9364101694132948 | `final.metric.random_lowrank_score` |\n+| Information-selected ridge | 0.9482262260487015 | `final.metric.selected_ridge_score` |\n+| Correlation-medoid ridge | 0.9327472829724573 | `final.metric.medoid_ridge_score` |\n+| Mean-offset | 0.920605668187274 | `final.metric.copy_score` |\n+| Historical means | 0.90687688776656 | `final.metric.constant_score` |\n+\n+The supplied paired family-clustered interval **against random-query low-rank only** is [0.014807167765235746, 0.01847801943997085], grounded in `final.metric.paired_gain_ci_low` and `final.metric.paired_gain_ci_high`. Explain its fixed resampling definition from the final plan. Do not recalculate it from seed means or attach it to another comparator or subgroup. Other baseline differences are observed-score comparisons, not established statistical superiority.\n+\n+Retain the local reversal: for Open LLM, family split, seed 1019, the studied score is 0.9531041725072664 versus 0.9533160599665489 for information-selected ridge (`final.evidence.episodes`). The method is not best in every retained cell.\n+\n+The source-level pooled scores are 0.9468974985138557 for MTEB and 0.9586298797315429 for Open LLM (`final.metric.mteb_score`, `final.metric.open_llm_score`). They have different task and budget regimes; do not interpret their difference as a controlled source-difficulty result.\n+\n+### Historical-dependence control\n+\n+Compare actual and independently column-deranged historical training with paired seeds within each source/split. The pooled deranged score is 0.9233917542059907, with an actual-minus-deranged gap of 0.029371934916708625 (`final.metric.permuted_score`, `final.metric.corruption_gap`). This supports use of historical cross-benchmark alignment. It does not uniquely identify the acquisition rule as the cause, certify leakage absence, or establish arbitrary out-of-distribution generalization.\n+\n+### Essential limitations\n+\n+Put these in the body, not only after the references:\n+\n+- Query policies leave different target sets. Results compare the observed remaining-target objective, not prediction error on an identical untouched panel; there is no fixed-target control.\n+- The selector ignores purchased values. Do not claim response-adaptive query design.\n+- Historical-cell rank validation is not nested held-out-family validation. Name-family grouping is heuristic and may miss cross-namespace lineages.\n+- Leaderboard missingness is observational and potentially selective. Missing entries are not measured targets or measured failures.\n+- The two independent source fits do not demonstrate transfer across domains. MTEB studies embedding tasks; Open LLM covers its own small benchmark suite.\n+- No universal sufficient budget, tolerance-defined sufficient budget, actual benchmark-inference savings, new-model inference run, rank sweep, missingness sweep, calibration experiment, or nonlinear-method victory is established.\n+- Execution/replay checks and reported qualification do not remove these scientific limitations.\n+\n+Budget evidence belongs in a substantive supplementary table: retained studied-method checkpoint arrays only, mapped to MTEB budgets 1/2/4/8 and Open LLM budgets 1/2/3 using the frozen plan. Do not invent baseline checkpoint curves or a threshold answering how large a budget is universally enough.\n+\n+## Required Figures and Layout\n+\n+Inspected `.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex` and local `paper.sty`: the document is an `article` with **one column, 5.5in text width, and 9in text height**. Full text width is also the column width; this is not a two-column conference layout. All three figures target `1.0'\"\\\\textwidth\"'`. A nominal 0.48-width figure would be an inset, not an ordinary conference column, and is too narrow for the planned labels.\n+\n+### Figure 1: Score-matrix mechanism overview\n+\n+- **Purpose:** immediate glance value for the object and mechanism, including the boundary between query choice and observed-score conditioning.\n+- **Type/generator:** qualitative `diagram`, `generate-concept-figure`; the only figure assigned that generator.\n+- **Content:** incomplete historical matrix → masked factor estimation → budgeted query set and purchased values → remaining-score reconstruction. Use separate arrows to show that purchased values update prediction, not selection. A short footer distinguishes source-specific fits and the two split regimes. Symbolic matrix cells are allowed; invented numeric pseudo-results are not.\n+- **Placement/footprint:** page 1 or 2, approximately 5.5 × 1.7in before caption; roughly one quarter page including caption.\n+- **Readability budget:** one panel, one panel per row, at most six labeled elements, at most three arrow/semantic styles, minimum 9pt rendered text. Full width is needed for the four-part information flow.\n+- **Grounding:** `final.evidence.episodes`, `study.selection_kind`; implementation provenance is the staged selected source and frozen final plan. No metric is plotted.\n+\n+### Figure 2: Source- and split-stratified method comparison\n+\n+- **Type/generator:** horizontal dot plot, matplotlib.\n+- **Content:** source-by-split 2 × 2 grid. Each panel has six abbreviated method rows, three seed dots, and a distinct mean marker. Use a shared expansion key and consistent score-axis meaning. This uses actual, nonreplay case scores from `final.evidence.episodes` only.\n+- **Placement/footprint:** results section; 5.5 × approximately 3.7in before caption, roughly half a page including caption. Each panel needs both readable method names and a meaningful score scale; do not shrink the whole figure to an inset.\n+- **Readability budget:** four total panels, two per row, six categories per panel, four series maximum counting the mean; minimum 8.5pt rendered text. Explicitly label any nonzero axis limits; dots avoid truncated-bar exaggeration.\n+- **Uncertainty:** seed dots show observed variation, not confidence intervals. The supplied pooled interval belongs in the pooled table/text, not on these subgroup points.\n+\n+### Figure 3: Dependence on historical alignment\n+\n+- **Type/generator:** paired-condition dot plot, matplotlib.\n+- **Content:** two source panels; each shows model-disjoint and name-family-disjoint splits under actual versus column-deranged training. Pair the same seeds, omit replay, and use exactly two condition legend entries. Paired links mark a controlled comparison, not elapsed time.\n+- **Placement/footprint:** next to the dependence-control discussion; 5.5 × approximately 2.1in before caption, about 0.3 page including caption.\n+- **Readability budget:** two total panels, two per row, two categories per panel, two series per panel; minimum 8.5pt text. No additional baseline series.\n+- **Grounding:** `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.permuted_score`, `final.metric.corruption_gap`.\n+\n+None of the figures is a search trajectory or milestone plot. Do not add a required budget curve when comparator checkpoint values are absent. A compact pooled table and a small protocol table complement the figures without duplicating their visual comparisons.\n+\n+**Vector-first export:** quantitative source must emit PDF and 300-DPI PNG; LaTeX must use PDF whenever available. Keep the concept diagram editable in draw.io and export PDF. Raster-only full-width assets require at least 2400px width; any genuine column-width alternative requires at least 1200px. Regenerate from source rather than upscale. Simplify labels/panels if final-size text fails the stated budgets.\n+\n+## Body-Page Plan\n+\n+Follow `VENUE.md`: ICLR 2026, anonymized review submission, **8–9 body pages excluding references**, with the last page at least 75% full if the body occupies eight pages. Target 8.5 pages. The allocations already include figures and tables:\n+\n+| Material | Target pages | Scientific use of space |\n+| --- | ---: | --- |\n+| Title and abstract | 0.45 | Question, conditional evidence, key scope boundary. |\n+| Introduction and early overview | 1.05 | Budgeted evaluation problem, precise empirical contribution, domain distinction. |\n+| Related Work | 0.65 | Verified permitted low-rank/design context and benchmark-evaluation distinctions, not retrieval-list filler. |\n+| Problem and Scope | 0.65 | Historical masks, availability, purchased versus remaining targets, exact objective. |\n+| Masked Low-Rank Selection and Reconstruction | 1.65 | Objective, alternating updates, rank validation, conditional reconstruction, acquisition proxy and its limits. |\n+| Evaluation Design | 1.00 | Source-specific splits, five operational baselines, controls, weighting, supplied uncertainty. |\n+| Prediction and Historical-Dependence Results | 1.80 | Two direct comparison figures, compact pooled table, heterogeneity and local reversal. |\n+| Discussion and Limitations | 0.95 | Method-dependent targets, selective missingness, family heuristics, restricted inference about budgets. |\n+| Conclusion | 0.30 | One conditional conclusion; no new claim. |\n+\n+Use any layout slack for clearer equations, baseline definitions, and target-policy/uncertainty explanation. Do not pad with unmeasured proposals, repeated pooled scores, broad surveys, operational logs, or speculative experiments. If evidence cannot fill the requirement substantively after typesetting, report that limitation rather than invent content.\n+\n+The supplied template scaffold contains an identifying author and a final-copy command. The later writer must remove identifying manuscript content, follow review formatting, preserve the orchestrator watermark, and omit acknowledgements/funding. Do not assert that the locally staged style has been independently verified as the latest official release. A separate **LLM Usage** section is required and may be after the references.\n+\n+## Supplementary Information After References\n+\n+**Purpose:** provide reproducible method/protocol depth and complete retained evidence without hiding anything essential to the thesis. The JSON gives the following exact planned subsection headings and grounding IDs.\n+\n+1. **Masked Factor Estimation and Conditional Querying.** Expand the inspected equations, fixed means, zero-filled centered initialization, alternating ridge updates, rank selection, and exact acquisition proxy. The current-target proxy includes the candidate coordinate; do not describe it as pure off-diagonal risk reduction or an MAE-optimal theorem. A rank-one covariance identity can explain the code, not prove empirical optimality. IDs: `study.selection_kind`, `final.evidence.episodes`; staged source provides implementation provenance.\n+2. **Pinned Data Extraction, Grouping, and Reproduction.** Use existing audit/plan/contract/requirements for revisions, extraction, deduplication, masks, heuristic families, budgets, environment and exact reproduction commands. Do not invent script names, observed storage, or runtime measurements. Register audit/plan linkage before asserting extra quantitative dataset counts. Respect Open LLM'\"'s undeclared dataset license and reacquisition rather than asserted redistribution rights. IDs: \"'`study.selection_kind`, `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.qualification.status`.\n+3. **Complete Seed, Split, and Budget Tables.** All nonreplay actual/control scores, five baseline scores, and studied checkpoint arrays; no invented comparator checkpoint values or new experiment. Retain the local ridge reversal and distinguish seed variation from confidence intervals. ID: `final.evidence.episodes`.\n+4. **Aggregation, Uncertainty, and Evaluation Boundaries.** Frozen weighting and family-clustered paired uncertainty; no interval reconstructed from seed means. Explain unavailable fixed targets, heuristic families, selective missingness, historical-cell validation and limited validity checks. IDs: `final.metric.paired_gain_ci_low`, `final.metric.paired_gain_ci_high`, `final.metric.reset_replay_ok`, `final.qualification.outcome`, `final.evidence.episodes`.\n+5. **Unmeasured Alternatives and Evaluation Provenance.** Brief selection/failure disclosure without an alternative-method leaderboard. Record unchanged original-baseline selection, zero measured search change, three missing scores, unknown failure causes, and independent final completion/qualification. IDs: `study.selection_kind`, `study.investigation_outcome`, `study.search_score_delta`, `study.attempts.total`, `study.attempts.scored`, `study.attempts.unscored`, `final.qualification.status`, `final.qualification.outcome`, `final.qualification.correct`. Translate machine fields into reader-facing language.\n+6. **LLM Usage.** Describe documented agent-assisted ideation/implementation and framing/writing precisely; distinguish unscored alternatives from evaluated retained code. Do not invent human supervision, literature verification, or experiments. The writer must add its actual subsequent role. IDs: `study.attempts.total`, `study.attempts.unscored`, `study.selection_kind`; the current task also documents the framing-agent role.\n+\n+Later authoritative appendix rankings can route additional grounded material here; do not modify the strategy retroactively or move essential counterevidence out of the body.\n+\n+## Literature and Claim Discipline\n+\n+The current `references.bib` and `references_provenance.json` contain factorization-related metadata but not the allowed starter/dataset records needed for a grounded domain review. Retrieval metadata alone does not establish that the paper was read, that it is relevant, or that any novelty contrast is supported. Do not cite unrelated applications merely to fill the bibliography. Before final writing, resolve genuinely needed allowed records with exact permitted titles/identifiers, verify provenance and content, and cite only keys actually present in the bibliography. Never infer the identity of the forbidden prior paper, search for it, or expand citation graphs; stop and log any accidental exposure. This framing stage performs no network lookup.\n+\n+Keep reader-facing prose free of private pipeline terms and paths. Distinguish an observed pooled advantage from a statistically supported paired contrast, a useful implementation identity from a new theorem, and publication eligibility from scientific qualification. No newly invented experiment or citation is needed to make this conditional empirical story coherent.\n+\n+## Wording to Reject\n+\n+Forbidden headings: **Search Progression; Campaign Phases; Milestones; First Successful Run; Experiment A / Experiment B; Candidate Leaderboard; From Baseline to Winner; Correctness and Eligibility.**\n+\n+Forbidden visible phrases: **we then tried; first valid result; subsequent improvements; next-best candidate; winning search method; all alternatives performed worse; correctness rate; correct and eligible; eligible; worker_01; worker_02; combined_score; rubric; state of the art; response-adaptive benchmark selection; a universal sufficient number of benchmarks; proved leakage-free; significantly better than every baseline.** Source identifiers appearing in this private memo are not recommendations for manuscript wording.\n+\n+This stage writes only the strategy artifacts and append-only memory. It does not draft `paper.tex`, write `claims_grounding.json`, generate final figures, run experiments, or run final-paper validation.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n)\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'apply_patch() { codex --codex-run-as-apply-patch \"$1\"; }\napply_patch \"$(cat <<'\"'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /workspace/paper/paper_strategy.json\n+{\n+  \\\"status\\\": \\\"ready\\\",\n+  \\\"selected_prompt_family\\\": \\\"paper_standalone\\\",\n+  \\\"recommended_title\\\": \\\"Variance-Guided Benchmark Selection with Masked Low-Rank Score Models\\\",\n+  \\\"central_question\\\": \\\"Under limited benchmark-query budgets, how well does variance-guided selection with masked low-rank reconstruction predict held-out models' remaining observed scores across model-disjoint and name-family-disjoint leaderboard splits?\\\",\n+  \\\"central_thesis\\\": \\\"On the two pinned leaderboard matrices, the retained variance-guided low-rank method has a higher pooled remaining-target prediction score than the tested baselines and loses score under historical-column derangement, supporting a conditional empirical result rather than universal benchmark sufficiency, response-adaptive selection, or fixed-target superiority.\\\",\n+  \\\"narrative_rationale\\\": \\\"The strongest evidence is the sealed final comparison of one retained method against five operational baselines across two sources, two split regimes, and three seeds, with a paired uncertainty interval against random-query low-rank prediction and a dependence-destroying control. Present MTEB embedding tasks and Open LLM generative-model benchmarks as separate evidence blocks under a shared score-matrix question; fit each source independently, without cross-source model alignment or transfer claims. The contribution is a transparent empirical assessment and reproducible mechanism description, not a newly discovered winning architecture. The alternatives have no measured performance evidence. The informative limitations, especially method-dependent remaining targets and non-response-adaptive selection, belong in the central argument rather than only in the supplement.\\\",\n+  \\\"prior_paper_story_status\\\": \\\"rejected\\\",\n+  \\\"edit_framing_decision\\\": \\\"Fresh framing, not an edit: no resolved edit-context files, previous_paper manuscript, aggregated directory, or extra_tasks directory are staged. The status 'rejected' records that no inherited manuscript story is adopted; it does not reject a scientific result. Preserve-with-local-updates has no prior manuscript to preserve; broaden-to-a-shared-method-family is unsupported for the unscored alternative implementations; recenter-on-the-retained-evaluated-method is selected because it has direct final evidence. No old title or figure plan is carried forward.\\\",\n+  \\\"staged_input_impact\\\": [\n+    \\\"Direct inspection of source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py establishes masked alternating ridge factors, historical-cell rank selection, conditional ridge reconstruction, and set-conditioned variance-reduction querying; purchased values affect prediction but not query choice.\\\",\n+    \\\"The staged selected and original-baseline source files are byte-identical. Study selection is the original baseline, not an improved search winner; do not manufacture a second final comparator for the same source.\\\",\n+    \\\"The final evidence supplies the actual scientific comparison despite the absence of scored search alternatives. The final qualification record is read independently of the downstream selection summary.\\\",\n+    \\\"The pinned final audit, plan, task contract, and evaluator's scoring/baseline definitions explain the two data domains, remaining-target score, heuristic family grouping, budgets, and bootstrap semantics. They are protocol provenance, not additional experimental results or substitute quantitative grounding IDs.\\\",\n+    \\\"The current bibliography/provenance contains retrieved factorization-related metadata but lacks the permitted starter and dataset records needed for domain positioning. This limits literature claims, not the coherence of the measured comparison; the writer must verify relevant allowed records before citing them and must not fill pages with unrelated retrieval hits. No network retrieval is performed in this framing stage.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"method_groups\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Variance-guided masked low-rank reconstruction\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"proposed\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"The single studied method. Describe 'proposed' only as the contract role, not a novelty or search-improvement claim. The retained source learns masked factors and selects queries using a conditional trace-reduction proxy. Ground performance in final.evidence.episodes and final.metric.combined_score.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Random-query masked low-rank reconstruction\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"ablation\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"The closest selector comparison: source inspection confirms the same factor-fitting and prediction construction with random available queries. A pooled paired family-clustered interval is available against this comparator; different remaining targets still prevent a fixed-target causal interpretation.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Information-selected covariance ridge\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Strongest pooled nonfactor comparator. It changes representation, regularization selection, and potentially query sets, so it is a joint pipeline comparison rather than a matched-query reconstruction ablation. Retain the Open LLM family-split seed where it slightly exceeds the studied method.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Correlation-medoid covariance ridge\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Tests a simpler correlation-centrality query ordering with covariance reconstruction; provides an interpretable selection comparator without adding an unevaluated method family.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Historical benchmark means\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Observation-invariant reference for the substantial predictability already present in historical task means. Its operational score is computed on its own query-policy remainder, not a universal zero-query target set.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Random-query mean-offset prediction\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Simple purchased-score reference: shift historical benchmark means by the observed mean residual. Distinguishes structured reconstruction from a global model-level offset.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"results_focus\\\": [\n+    \\\"Primary view: final noncontrol, nonreplay case scores for the six methods, stratified by source and split, with all three seed observations visible. Label the metric 'Normalized prediction score (1 - MAE; higher is better)', not percent accuracy or variance explained. Average only with the documented equal target/row/checkpoint/seed/split/source hierarchy.\\\",\n+    \\\"Pooled evidence: studied method 0.9527636891226994, random-query low-rank 0.9364101694132948, information-selected ridge 0.9482262260487015, medoid ridge 0.9327472829724573, mean-offset 0.920605668187274, and historical means 0.90687688776656. Use a compact table, not a redundant figure. Only the studied-versus-random-low-rank comparison has a supplied paired interval: [0.014807167765235746, 0.01847801943997085]. Do not attach that interval to another comparator or a source/split cell.\\\",\n+    \\\"Source evidence remains distinct: MTEB pooled score 0.9468974985138557 and Open LLM pooled score 0.9586298797315429 describe different task and budget regimes, not a controlled difficulty comparison. MTEB is embedding-model evidence, not evidence about generative LLM benchmark suites.\\\",\n+    \\\"Dependence control: compare actual and independently column-deranged historical training scores for each source/split with paired seeds; pooled deranged score 0.9233917542059907 and actual-minus-deranged score 0.029371934916708625. The control supports dependence on historical alignment, not unique causal attribution to the acquisition rule or immunity to leakage.\\\",\n+    \\\"Qualification for claims: the factor method is not best in every retained cell. In Open LLM family split seed 1019, its 0.9531041725072664 is below information-selected ridge's 0.9533160599665489. Report this local reversal and avoid blanket or significant-superiority claims over all baselines.\\\",\n+    \\\"Budget evidence is descriptive: retain existing studied-method checkpoint values as an appendix table, with actual budget labels taken from the frozen final plan. No per-budget baseline series, fixed-target scores, tolerance-defined sufficient-k result, new inference-cost measurements, or missingness-sweep results are available.\\\",\n+    \\\"Private-only provenance: study.selection_kind=baseline; study.investigation_outcome=completed_no_winner; study.search_score_delta=0.0; study.attempts.total=3, scored=0, unscored=3. These establish no measured search gain and no comparative losses for alternative methods. Search and final scores must not be subtracted as improvement.\\\",\n+    \\\"Private-only qualification: final.qualification.status=completed, final.qualification.outcome=qualified, final.qualification.correct=true. There is no failed final qualification to disclose in this run. Detailed gate diagnostics are not supplied; qualification does not establish novelty, universal generalization, or validity of stronger scientific interpretations. Candidate diagnostics remain unverified.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_plan\\\": [\n+    \\\"Figure 1, early overview: sparse historical score matrix -> masked factor fit -> budgeted query set and purchased values -> remaining-score reconstruction, with distinct arrows showing that values update predictions but not selection; a small footer names the two source domains and two split regimes without numerical pseudo-results.\\\",\n+    \\\"Figure 2, main comparison: four horizontal dot-plot panels, arranged by source and split, compare all six evaluated methods using actual/nonreplay case scores; display three seed points and a clearly distinguished mean per method.\\\",\n+    \\\"Figure 3, dependence control: two source panels compare actual versus column-deranged historical training in each split using paired seed observations; use no training-time or search-trajectory axis.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_specs\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"concept_overview\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Make the score-matrix object, query/prediction mechanism, and boundaries of the evidence legible before the numerical comparisons.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"diagram\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"generate-concept-figure\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"information_flow\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"none; qualitative mechanism only\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"independent source-specific fits, not merged datasets\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"The inspected ICLR article template and paper.sty are single-column with 5.5in text width and 9in text height. Target 5.5 x 1.7in before caption, approximately one quarter page including caption, on page 1 or 2. Use one left-to-right schematic with at most six short labeled elements and 9pt minimum final text; a half-width inset would force small matrix labels. Any example cells use masks or symbolic values, never invented measured scores.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 6,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"study.selection_kind\\\"],\n+      \\\"implementation_provenance\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py\\\", \\\"task/resources/final/plan.json\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"main_comparison\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Show the direct six-method comparison and its source/split/seed heterogeneity, including the retained local reversal.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"horizontal_dot_plot\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"six evaluated method labels\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"normalized prediction score (1 - MAE), averaged across available checkpoints within each case\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"source by model-disjoint or name-family-disjoint split\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Target the actual single-column full text width, 5.5in, with a 2-by-2 grid approximately 3.7in tall before caption and at least 8.5pt final labels. Budget roughly half a body page including caption. Use short method labels with a shared expansion key, six horizontal rows per panel, and common score-axis semantics. Show three seed markers plus one mean marker, not six overlapping colored lines. A 0.48-textwidth placement would leave too little space for method labels and score differences. If a nonzero axis range is used, show it explicitly and use dots, not truncated bars.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 6,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"data_filter\\\": \\\"Keep control=false and replay=false only; do not double-count the first-seed replay; derive displayed means transparently from the retained episode scores, without treating them as new experiments.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"historical_dependence_control\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Expose how scores change when historical cross-benchmark correspondence is disrupted, with source and split heterogeneity visible.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"paired_condition_dot_plot\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"model-disjoint and name-family-disjoint split\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"normalized prediction score (1 - MAE)\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"MTEB embedding models versus Open LLM generative models\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Use two side-by-side source panels at the inspected 5.5in text width, approximately 2.1in tall before caption and 8.5pt minimum final text; reserve about 0.3 body page including caption. Two conditions and two split categories fit without rotating labels. Link paired seed observations only to mark the controlled contrast, not temporal progression. Do not shrink to half width or add five baseline control series.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.permuted_score\\\", \\\"final.metric.corruption_gap\\\"],\n+      \\\"data_filter\\\": \\\"Pair actual/control cases by source, split, and seed; exclude replay; use actual and column-deranged as the only condition legend entries.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"supplementary_plan\\\": {\n+    \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"After the references, provide reproducible implementation and protocol depth plus the complete retained numerical evidence, without moving central caveats, the main baseline contrast, or the dependence control out of the body.\\\",\n+    \\\"planned_subsections\\\": [\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Masked Factor Estimation and Conditional Querying\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Expand the inspected source into the masked squared-error/ridge objective, fixed column means, zero-filled centered initialization, alternating ridge updates, historical-cell rank selection, conditional prediction, and exact acquisition proxy. Explain that selection ignores observed values and includes the candidate coordinate in its current-target trace proxy. An algebraic rank-one covariance identity may explain the implementation; do not invent a recovery, optimality, or MAE guarantee. Use the staged source as implementation provenance, not as measured evidence of superiority.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"study.selection_kind\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Pinned Data Extraction, Grouping, and Reproduction\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Document the already-staged audit, plan, task contract, environment requirements, exact public source revisions, score extraction and bounds, deduplication, historical-only feature construction, heuristic name-family links, and checkpoint budgets. Preserve MTEB versus generative-model distinctions and the undeclared Open LLM dataset-license limitation. Provide exact rerun and table/figure-generation commands from the available implementation; do not invent scripts, measured storage, or timings. Treat audit/plan metadata as protocol provenance and register its evidence linkage before claiming any extra numerical dataset counts.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"study.selection_kind\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.qualification.status\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Complete Seed, Split, and Budget Tables\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Tabulate every nonreplay actual and control case, all five available baseline scores, and the studied method's retained checkpoint arrays. Map checkpoint positions to the frozen plan; do not infer absent per-budget baseline values. Include the local information-selected-ridge reversal. Mark seed variation as observed variation, not an independent-sample confidence interval, and state that missing cells were not prediction targets.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Aggregation, Uncertainty, and Evaluation Boundaries\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Explain equal aggregation weights and the supplied paired family-clustered bootstrap interval against random-query low-rank prediction, using the fixed plan's resampling definition. Retain the supplied interval rather than recomputing it from seed means. Describe remaining-target policy differences, absence of fixed-target controls, heuristic family labels, observational missingness, historical-cell rather than nested family validation, and lack of uncertainty for other baseline contrasts. Separate execution/replay checks from broader scientific validity.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.metric.paired_gain_ci_low\\\", \\\"final.metric.paired_gain_ci_high\\\", \\\"final.metric.reset_replay_ok\\\", \\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Unmeasured Alternatives and Evaluation Provenance\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Briefly disclose that the retained source was the original baseline, no search-score change was measured, and all alternative attempts lack scores. Their recorded execution failures have unknown causes and do not establish inferiority or a diagnosed validity/adaptivity defect. Preserve independent final completion/qualification facts and distinguish search from final evaluation; keep machine field names and local paths out of reader-facing prose. Do not create an alternative-method leaderboard.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"study.selection_kind\\\", \\\"study.investigation_outcome\\\", \\\"study.search_score_delta\\\", \\\"study.attempts.total\\\", \\\"study.attempts.scored\\\", \\\"study.attempts.unscored\\\", \\\"final.qualification.status\\\", \\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\", \\\"final.qualification.correct\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"LLM Usage\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Disclose the documented role of LLM agents in alternative-method ideation/implementation and this framing/writing workflow. Distinguish unscored generated alternatives from evaluated retained code; do not assert that an LLM trained the evaluated models, ran unrecorded experiments, or independently verified literature. The writing-stage author must add its actual role without inventing undocumented human supervision.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"study.attempts.total\\\", \\\"study.attempts.unscored\\\", \\\"study.selection_kind\\\"]\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \\\"forbidden_headings\\\": [\n+    \\\"Search Progression\\\",\n+    \\\"Campaign Phases\\\",\n+    \\\"Milestones\\\",\n+    \\\"First Successful Run\\\",\n+    \\\"Experiment A / Experiment B\\\",\n+    \\\"Candidate Leaderboard\\\",\n+    \\\"From Baseline to Winner\\\",\n+    \\\"Correctness and Eligibility\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"forbidden_phrases\\\": [\n+    \\\"we then tried\\\",\n+    \\\"first valid result\\\",\n+    \\\"subsequent improvements\\\",\n+    \\\"next-best candidate\\\",\n+    \\\"winning search method\\\",\n+    \\\"all alternatives performed worse\\\",\n+    \\\"correctness rate\\\",\n+    \\\"correct and eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_01\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_02\\\",\n+    \\\"combined_score\\\",\n+    \\\"rubric\\\",\n+    \\\"state of the art\\\",\n+    \\\"response-adaptive benchmark selection\\\",\n+    \\\"a universal sufficient number of benchmarks\\\",\n+    \\\"proved leakage-free\\\",\n+    \\\"significantly better than every baseline\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"notes_for_writer\\\": [\n+    \\\"The memo and source identifiers are private planning material. Reader-facing prose should use named methods, normalized prediction score, model-disjoint/name-family-disjoint splits, and column-deranged history. Do not expose machine-native metric labels, selection machinery, or local infrastructure paths.\\\",\n+    \\\"Private-only grounding ledger: primary metrics use final.metric.* and cases use final.evidence.episodes. Selection, search-score equality/delta, and attempt counts use study.*. Qualification uses final.qualification.* exclusively, not study.final.* or search execution flags. These records report completed/qualified/true in this run; do not invent a qualification failure or infer missing gate details. A later outcome change must propagate through draft, review, audit, and revision, not be hidden by retained metrics.\\\",\n+    \\\"Main-body structure and inclusive page targets: title/abstract 0.45 page; Introduction with early overview 1.05; Related Work 0.65; Problem and Scope 0.65; Masked Low-Rank Selection and Reconstruction 1.65; Evaluation Design 1.0; Prediction and Historical-Dependence Results 1.8; Discussion and Limitations 0.95; Conclusion 0.30. Total target 8.5 body pages, with figures/tables included in those allocations, not added afterward. The hard venue range is 8-9 pages excluding references; an 8-page body needs its last page at least 75% full. Use extra space for equations, baseline definitions, aggregation and target-policy explanation, not unmeasured experiments or broad literature filler.\\\",\n+    \\\"The template is single-column: column width and full text width are both 5.5in, not a two-column 0.48-textwidth convention. Use ordinary figure environments at the planned full width. Text height is 9in. The supplied paper.tex scaffold has an identifying author and final-copy command: the future writer must anonymize it and use review formatting as required by VENUE.md, preserve the orchestrator watermark, and not claim the locally staged style has been independently verified as the latest official release.\\\",\n+    \\\"Report the objective exactly: clip predictions to [0,1], score only available unpurchased entries, and average absolute errors within each model before the frozen hierarchy. High scores are not classification accuracy, percent of benchmarks recovered, calibrated uncertainty, or explained variance. Querying changes the target set; observed objectives cannot establish error reduction on an identical held-out panel.\\\",\n+    \\\"A mechanistic account may derive the implemented conditional covariance/ridge equations under a working linear model. Explicitly distinguish the acquisition trace proxy from MAE optimality and from a pure off-diagonal target-risk criterion. The studied selector is sequential but does not depend on purchased score values. Do not attribute it to the unscored overlap-shrunk, latent-mixture, or monotone-skill proposals.\\\",\n+    \\\"No new ablations, fixed-target evaluations, family-validation results, nonlinear wins, rank-sensitivity sweeps, calibration curves, real benchmark execution savings, GPU comparisons, or universal k thresholds may be planned as completed evidence. Budget tables answer only what the retained checkpoint scores show; no error-tolerance target was prespecified.\\\",\n+    \\\"The supplied paired interval supports only the pooled comparison with random-query low-rank prediction under the observed objective. For all other comparisons use observed-score language and display seed variability without inventing p-values or confidence intervals. Do not count replay as a fourth seed or assume three seeds are independent model families.\\\",\n+    \\\"Historical derangement preserves marginal/missingness structure while disrupting row correspondence; a score drop supports use of cross-benchmark alignment, not proof of a unique mechanism, generalization to arbitrary models, or an exhaustive validity audit. Family links are naming heuristics; MTEB and Open LLM are independent source-specific fits.\\\",\n+    \\\"Keep all central comparisons, the actual-versus-deranged control, and essential caveats in the main text. Route full case/checkpoint tables, expanded equations, acquisition/environment details and documented unmeasured alternatives after references under Supplementary Information. Any later authoritative appendix ranking may add material there without changing this strategy.\\\",\n+    \\\"Vector-first contract: quantitative generators must export both PDF and PNG from the same source, PNG at 300 DPI; LaTeX must include PDF whenever available. Preserve editable draw.io and PDF exports for the concept overview. If raster-only is unavoidable, regenerate from source at least 2400px wide for these full-width figures, or 1200px for any genuine column-width alternative; never upscale an existing raster. Inspect final-size labels and simplify rather than shrink. Use at most one generate-concept-figure diagram.\\\",\n+    \\\"Literature guardrail: the current retrieved metadata is not a read/verified domain literature review. Cite only relevant keys actually present in references.bib after checking their provenance and permitted content. Missing starter/data records require narrowly scoped exact-title or exact-identifier resolution and actual reading before citation; never search for the forbidden prior study, traverse citation graphs, guess its identity, or invent missing entries. Log and stop reading any incidental forbidden material. Do not import the retrieval list's unrelated application papers merely to satisfy page count.\\\",\n+    \\\"Contribution wording should emphasize a reproducible empirical study of a retained method and operational limits, not a new architecture or search success. Publication-format compliance is separate from scientific qualification. No final manuscript, evidence-claim map, final-paper validation, or new experiments are produced in this strategy stage.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"failure_reason\\\": \\\"\\\"\n+}\n*** Add File: /workspace/paper/paper_strategy.md\n+# Paper Framing Strategy\n+\n+## Decision\n+\n+**Status: ready.** Use \"'`paper_standalone` and the `write-paper-standalone` family. Provisional title: **Variance-Guided Benchmark Selection with Masked Low-Rank Score Models**.\n+\n+**Central question:** Under limited benchmark-query budgets, how well does variance-guided selection with masked low-rank reconstruction predict held-out models'\"' remaining observed scores across model-disjoint and name-family-disjoint leaderboard splits?\n+\n+**Central thesis:** On the two pinned leaderboard matrices, the retained variance-guided low-rank method has a higher pooled remaining-target prediction score than the tested baselines and loses score under historical-column derangement, supporting a conditional empirical result rather than universal benchmark sufficiency, response-adaptive selection, or fixed-target superiority.\n+\n+This is an empirical assessment of one retained method, not a story about inventing a winning architecture. MTEB embedding models and Open LLM generative models form **separate evidence blocks under one score-matrix question**. Fit and discuss them independently; do not claim cross-source transfer, merge their model identities, or treat embedding tasks as generative-model benchmarks.\n+\n+## Framing Alternatives and Staged Inputs\n+\n+No resolved edit-context files, prior manuscript, \"'`aggregated/`, or `extra_tasks/` are staged. `prior_paper_story_status` is `rejected`: no inherited story is adopted, not a rejection of an old scientific result.\n+\n+- **Preserve with local updates:** inapplicable because there is no prior manuscript to preserve.\n+- **Broaden to a shared alternative-method family:** rejected because overlap-shrunk covariance, latent mixtures, and monotone-skill alternatives have no measured performance evidence.\n+- **Recenter on the retained evaluated method:** selected because it alone has final evidence with meaningful baseline, split, seed, and corruption comparisons.\n+- **Center a negative search-results paper:** weaker than the selected framing. Unscored alternatives do not establish measured negative performance findings, whereas the retained method has an actual comparative evaluation.\n+\n+Direct inspection of `source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py` establishes masked alternating ridge factors, historical-cell rank selection, conditional ridge prediction, and a trace-reduction query proxy. The selected and original-baseline staged source files are byte-identical. The method is sequential and set-conditioned: purchased score values affect reconstruction **but not query choice**. It is not the response-adaptive mixture or the off-diagonal overlap-aware proposal.\n+\n+The frozen audit and plan under `task/resources/final/`, the task contract, and the evaluator'\"'s score/baseline definitions provide protocol provenance. They do not substitute for registered numerical result sources. Do not assert equality between differently recorded whole-tree hashes merely from equality of the staged source files.\n+\n+## Private-Only Evidence Ledger\n+\n+This section is planning/audit context, not reader-facing vocabulary.\n+\n+- Read \"'`paper_data.json.final_evaluation` independently. `final.qualification.status` is `completed`, `final.qualification.outcome` is `qualified`, and `final.qualification.correct` is true. There is **no failed final qualification** to disclose in this run. Detailed gate diagnostics remain unavailable; successful completion does not establish scientific novelty or stronger validity claims. Candidate diagnostics are explicitly unverified.\n+- Selection uses `study.selection_kind=baseline` and `study.investigation_outcome=completed_no_winner`. Both search score and original-baseline score are 0.9527030000575736; `study.search_score_delta=0.0`.\n+- `study.attempts.total=3`, `study.attempts.scored=0`, and `study.attempts.unscored=3`. Unscored attempts are missing performance evidence, not measured losses. Their recorded execution-failure causes are unknown; neither inferiority nor a particular validity/adaptivity defect is diagnosed.\n+- Keep search and final scopes separate. Never subtract the search score from the final score and call it improvement. Do not display the frozen source as an improved replacement for its identical original baseline.\n+- Final case data come from `final.evidence.episodes`. The three final seeds are 1009, 1013, and 1019. Exclude control cases from primary comparisons and exclude the replay from every primary aggregate; replay is not a fourth seed.\n+- Qualification statements must map to `final.qualification.*`, not downstream mirrors or search flags. If later evidence changes the outcome, preserve the changed qualification and its limitations in drafting, review, audit, and revision.\n+\n+## Method Groups\n+\n+Keep exactly the six evaluated plot labels; group them scientifically rather than by discovery order.\n+\n+| Group | Role | Scientific purpose |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Variance-guided masked low-rank reconstruction | Studied method; `proposed` in the JSON contract only | Connect incomplete historical scores, conditional reconstruction, and variance-guided queries; do not imply new architecture or a search gain. |\n+| Random-query masked low-rank reconstruction | Selector ablation | Same factor-fitting/prediction construction, different query rule; closest comparison and only comparator with supplied pooled paired uncertainty. |\n+| Information-selected covariance ridge | Strong baseline | Closest pooled nonfactor comparator; representation, tuning, and queries can all differ, so not a matched-query prediction ablation. |\n+| Correlation-medoid covariance ridge | Simpler baseline | Historical correlation-centrality ordering with covariance reconstruction. |\n+| Historical benchmark means | Observation-invariant baseline | Expose predictable task marginals; its evaluated remainder still depends on its operational query policy. |\n+| Random-query mean-offset prediction | Simple observation-using baseline | Test whether a single model-level score offset explains the result. |\n+\n+Do not add unevaluated methods to the performance comparison. A short supplementary disclosure of alternatives is sufficient.\n+\n+## Results and Claim Boundaries\n+\n+### Primary comparison\n+\n+Show the six methods in each source-by-split condition, displaying every retained seed score. The reader-facing metric is **Normalized prediction score (1 − MAE; higher is better)**. Predictions are clipped to natural score bounds; errors are averaged over available, unpurchased entries within a model and then through the frozen checkpoint/seed/split/source hierarchy. This is not classification accuracy, explained variance, or the fraction of benchmarks successfully recovered.\n+\n+The pooled scores below already exist in `paper_data.json`; use their `final.metric.*` sources in the eventual claim map.\n+\n+| Method | Pooled score | Grounding ID |\n+| --- | ---: | --- |\n+| Variance-guided masked low-rank | 0.9527636891226994 | `final.metric.combined_score` |\n+| Random-query masked low-rank | 0.9364101694132948 | `final.metric.random_lowrank_score` |\n+| Information-selected ridge | 0.9482262260487015 | `final.metric.selected_ridge_score` |\n+| Correlation-medoid ridge | 0.9327472829724573 | `final.metric.medoid_ridge_score` |\n+| Mean-offset | 0.920605668187274 | `final.metric.copy_score` |\n+| Historical means | 0.90687688776656 | `final.metric.constant_score` |\n+\n+The supplied paired family-clustered interval **against random-query low-rank only** is [0.014807167765235746, 0.01847801943997085], grounded in `final.metric.paired_gain_ci_low` and `final.metric.paired_gain_ci_high`. Explain its fixed resampling definition from the final plan. Do not recalculate it from seed means or attach it to another comparator or subgroup. Other baseline differences are observed-score comparisons, not established statistical superiority.\n+\n+Retain the local reversal: for Open LLM, family split, seed 1019, the studied score is 0.9531041725072664 versus 0.9533160599665489 for information-selected ridge (`final.evidence.episodes`). The method is not best in every retained cell.\n+\n+The source-level pooled scores are 0.9468974985138557 for MTEB and 0.9586298797315429 for Open LLM (`final.metric.mteb_score`, `final.metric.open_llm_score`). They have different task and budget regimes; do not interpret their difference as a controlled source-difficulty result.\n+\n+### Historical-dependence control\n+\n+Compare actual and independently column-deranged historical training with paired seeds within each source/split. The pooled deranged score is 0.9233917542059907, with an actual-minus-deranged gap of 0.029371934916708625 (`final.metric.permuted_score`, `final.metric.corruption_gap`). This supports use of historical cross-benchmark alignment. It does not uniquely identify the acquisition rule as the cause, certify leakage absence, or establish arbitrary out-of-distribution generalization.\n+\n+### Essential limitations\n+\n+Put these in the body, not only after the references:\n+\n+- Query policies leave different target sets. Results compare the observed remaining-target objective, not prediction error on an identical untouched panel; there is no fixed-target control.\n+- The selector ignores purchased values. Do not claim response-adaptive query design.\n+- Historical-cell rank validation is not nested held-out-family validation. Name-family grouping is heuristic and may miss cross-namespace lineages.\n+- Leaderboard missingness is observational and potentially selective. Missing entries are not measured targets or measured failures.\n+- The two independent source fits do not demonstrate transfer across domains. MTEB studies embedding tasks; Open LLM covers its own small benchmark suite.\n+- No universal sufficient budget, tolerance-defined sufficient budget, actual benchmark-inference savings, new-model inference run, rank sweep, missingness sweep, calibration experiment, or nonlinear-method victory is established.\n+- Execution/replay checks and reported qualification do not remove these scientific limitations.\n+\n+Budget evidence belongs in a substantive supplementary table: retained studied-method checkpoint arrays only, mapped to MTEB budgets 1/2/4/8 and Open LLM budgets 1/2/3 using the frozen plan. Do not invent baseline checkpoint curves or a threshold answering how large a budget is universally enough.\n+\n+## Required Figures and Layout\n+\n+Inspected `.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex` and local `paper.sty`: the document is an `article` with **one column, 5.5in text width, and 9in text height**. Full text width is also the column width; this is not a two-column conference layout. All three figures target `1.0'\"\\\\textwidth\"'`. A nominal 0.48-width figure would be an inset, not an ordinary conference column, and is too narrow for the planned labels.\n+\n+### Figure 1: Score-matrix mechanism overview\n+\n+- **Purpose:** immediate glance value for the object and mechanism, including the boundary between query choice and observed-score conditioning.\n+- **Type/generator:** qualitative `diagram`, `generate-concept-figure`; the only figure assigned that generator.\n+- **Content:** incomplete historical matrix → masked factor estimation → budgeted query set and purchased values → remaining-score reconstruction. Use separate arrows to show that purchased values update prediction, not selection. A short footer distinguishes source-specific fits and the two split regimes. Symbolic matrix cells are allowed; invented numeric pseudo-results are not.\n+- **Placement/footprint:** page 1 or 2, approximately 5.5 × 1.7in before caption; roughly one quarter page including caption.\n+- **Readability budget:** one panel, one panel per row, at most six labeled elements, at most three arrow/semantic styles, minimum 9pt rendered text. Full width is needed for the four-part information flow.\n+- **Grounding:** `final.evidence.episodes`, `study.selection_kind`; implementation provenance is the staged selected source and frozen final plan. No metric is plotted.\n+\n+### Figure 2: Source- and split-stratified method comparison\n+\n+- **Type/generator:** horizontal dot plot, matplotlib.\n+- **Content:** source-by-split 2 × 2 grid. Each panel has six abbreviated method rows, three seed dots, and a distinct mean marker. Use a shared expansion key and consistent score-axis meaning. This uses actual, nonreplay case scores from `final.evidence.episodes` only.\n+- **Placement/footprint:** results section; 5.5 × approximately 3.7in before caption, roughly half a page including caption. Each panel needs both readable method names and a meaningful score scale; do not shrink the whole figure to an inset.\n+- **Readability budget:** four total panels, two per row, six categories per panel, four series maximum counting the mean; minimum 8.5pt rendered text. Explicitly label any nonzero axis limits; dots avoid truncated-bar exaggeration.\n+- **Uncertainty:** seed dots show observed variation, not confidence intervals. The supplied pooled interval belongs in the pooled table/text, not on these subgroup points.\n+\n+### Figure 3: Dependence on historical alignment\n+\n+- **Type/generator:** paired-condition dot plot, matplotlib.\n+- **Content:** two source panels; each shows model-disjoint and name-family-disjoint splits under actual versus column-deranged training. Pair the same seeds, omit replay, and use exactly two condition legend entries. Paired links mark a controlled comparison, not elapsed time.\n+- **Placement/footprint:** next to the dependence-control discussion; 5.5 × approximately 2.1in before caption, about 0.3 page including caption.\n+- **Readability budget:** two total panels, two per row, two categories per panel, two series per panel; minimum 8.5pt text. No additional baseline series.\n+- **Grounding:** `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.permuted_score`, `final.metric.corruption_gap`.\n+\n+None of the figures is a search trajectory or milestone plot. Do not add a required budget curve when comparator checkpoint values are absent. A compact pooled table and a small protocol table complement the figures without duplicating their visual comparisons.\n+\n+**Vector-first export:** quantitative source must emit PDF and 300-DPI PNG; LaTeX must use PDF whenever available. Keep the concept diagram editable in draw.io and export PDF. Raster-only full-width assets require at least 2400px width; any genuine column-width alternative requires at least 1200px. Regenerate from source rather than upscale. Simplify labels/panels if final-size text fails the stated budgets.\n+\n+## Body-Page Plan\n+\n+Follow `VENUE.md`: ICLR 2026, anonymized review submission, **8–9 body pages excluding references**, with the last page at least 75% full if the body occupies eight pages. Target 8.5 pages. The allocations already include figures and tables:\n+\n+| Material | Target pages | Scientific use of space |\n+| --- | ---: | --- |\n+| Title and abstract | 0.45 | Question, conditional evidence, key scope boundary. |\n+| Introduction and early overview | 1.05 | Budgeted evaluation problem, precise empirical contribution, domain distinction. |\n+| Related Work | 0.65 | Verified permitted low-rank/design context and benchmark-evaluation distinctions, not retrieval-list filler. |\n+| Problem and Scope | 0.65 | Historical masks, availability, purchased versus remaining targets, exact objective. |\n+| Masked Low-Rank Selection and Reconstruction | 1.65 | Objective, alternating updates, rank validation, conditional reconstruction, acquisition proxy and its limits. |\n+| Evaluation Design | 1.00 | Source-specific splits, five operational baselines, controls, weighting, supplied uncertainty. |\n+| Prediction and Historical-Dependence Results | 1.80 | Two direct comparison figures, compact pooled table, heterogeneity and local reversal. |\n+| Discussion and Limitations | 0.95 | Method-dependent targets, selective missingness, family heuristics, restricted inference about budgets. |\n+| Conclusion | 0.30 | One conditional conclusion; no new claim. |\n+\n+Use any layout slack for clearer equations, baseline definitions, and target-policy/uncertainty explanation. Do not pad with unmeasured proposals, repeated pooled scores, broad surveys, operational logs, or speculative experiments. If evidence cannot fill the requirement substantively after typesetting, report that limitation rather than invent content.\n+\n+The supplied template scaffold contains an identifying author and a final-copy command. The later writer must remove identifying manuscript content, follow review formatting, preserve the orchestrator watermark, and omit acknowledgements/funding. Do not assert that the locally staged style has been independently verified as the latest official release. A separate **LLM Usage** section is required and may be after the references.\n+\n+## Supplementary Information After References\n+\n+**Purpose:** provide reproducible method/protocol depth and complete retained evidence without hiding anything essential to the thesis. The JSON gives the following exact planned subsection headings and grounding IDs.\n+\n+1. **Masked Factor Estimation and Conditional Querying.** Expand the inspected equations, fixed means, zero-filled centered initialization, alternating ridge updates, rank selection, and exact acquisition proxy. The current-target proxy includes the candidate coordinate; do not describe it as pure off-diagonal risk reduction or an MAE-optimal theorem. A rank-one covariance identity can explain the code, not prove empirical optimality. IDs: `study.selection_kind`, `final.evidence.episodes`; staged source provides implementation provenance.\n+2. **Pinned Data Extraction, Grouping, and Reproduction.** Use existing audit/plan/contract/requirements for revisions, extraction, deduplication, masks, heuristic families, budgets, environment and exact reproduction commands. Do not invent script names, observed storage, or runtime measurements. Register audit/plan linkage before asserting extra quantitative dataset counts. Respect Open LLM'\"'s undeclared dataset license and reacquisition rather than asserted redistribution rights. IDs: \"'`study.selection_kind`, `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.qualification.status`.\n+3. **Complete Seed, Split, and Budget Tables.** All nonreplay actual/control scores, five baseline scores, and studied checkpoint arrays; no invented comparator checkpoint values or new experiment. Retain the local ridge reversal and distinguish seed variation from confidence intervals. ID: `final.evidence.episodes`.\n+4. **Aggregation, Uncertainty, and Evaluation Boundaries.** Frozen weighting and family-clustered paired uncertainty; no interval reconstructed from seed means. Explain unavailable fixed targets, heuristic families, selective missingness, historical-cell validation and limited validity checks. IDs: `final.metric.paired_gain_ci_low`, `final.metric.paired_gain_ci_high`, `final.metric.reset_replay_ok`, `final.qualification.outcome`, `final.evidence.episodes`.\n+5. **Unmeasured Alternatives and Evaluation Provenance.** Brief selection/failure disclosure without an alternative-method leaderboard. Record unchanged original-baseline selection, zero measured search change, three missing scores, unknown failure causes, and independent final completion/qualification. IDs: `study.selection_kind`, `study.investigation_outcome`, `study.search_score_delta`, `study.attempts.total`, `study.attempts.scored`, `study.attempts.unscored`, `final.qualification.status`, `final.qualification.outcome`, `final.qualification.correct`. Translate machine fields into reader-facing language.\n+6. **LLM Usage.** Describe documented agent-assisted ideation/implementation and framing/writing precisely; distinguish unscored alternatives from evaluated retained code. Do not invent human supervision, literature verification, or experiments. The writer must add its actual subsequent role. IDs: `study.attempts.total`, `study.attempts.unscored`, `study.selection_kind`; the current task also documents the framing-agent role.\n+\n+Later authoritative appendix rankings can route additional grounded material here; do not modify the strategy retroactively or move essential counterevidence out of the body.\n+\n+## Literature and Claim Discipline\n+\n+The current `references.bib` and `references_provenance.json` contain factorization-related metadata but not the allowed starter/dataset records needed for a grounded domain review. Retrieval metadata alone does not establish that the paper was read, that it is relevant, or that any novelty contrast is supported. Do not cite unrelated applications merely to fill the bibliography. Before final writing, resolve genuinely needed allowed records with exact permitted titles/identifiers, verify provenance and content, and cite only keys actually present in the bibliography. Never infer the identity of the forbidden prior paper, search for it, or expand citation graphs; stop and log any accidental exposure. This framing stage performs no network lookup.\n+\n+Keep reader-facing prose free of private pipeline terms and paths. Distinguish an observed pooled advantage from a statistically supported paired contrast, a useful implementation identity from a new theorem, and publication eligibility from scientific qualification. No newly invented experiment or citation is needed to make this conditional empirical story coherent.\n+\n+## Wording to Reject\n+\n+Forbidden headings: **Search Progression; Campaign Phases; Milestones; First Successful Run; Experiment A / Experiment B; Candidate Leaderboard; From Baseline to Winner; Correctness and Eligibility.**\n+\n+Forbidden visible phrases: **we then tried; first valid result; subsequent improvements; next-best candidate; winning search method; all alternatives performed worse; correctness rate; correct and eligible; eligible; worker_01; worker_02; combined_score; rubric; state of the art; response-adaptive benchmark selection; a universal sufficient number of benchmarks; proved leakage-free; significantly better than every baseline.** Source identifiers appearing in this private memo are not recommendations for manuscript wording.\n+\n+This stage writes only the strategy artifacts and append-only memory. It does not draft `paper.tex`, write `claims_grounding.json`, generate final figures, run experiments, or run final-paper validation.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n)\"'","aggregated_output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /workspace/paper/paper_strategy.json\nA /workspace/paper/paper_strategy.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
